commit 4138c23aa5c23e4b94745b6f3fc48b5b0a2e25cd

C03: the deictic-level question asks what to set, never the level already given (AUDIO1379)

AUDIO1375 measured the new deictic_level class: «Ponlo a 100 ahora» reached the clarification but the question asked «¿A qué nivel quieres ponerlo a 100?», and «devuelvelo a 100» got «¿A qué nivel quieres poner el volumen?» (the setting guessed, the level asked again).

llm.clarify_unresolved_input: for deictic_level the question must contain «qué/cuál» (what/which) and must not ask the level («a qué nivel», «cuánto», «how much»); one correction with the contract (the level is given, what is missing is which setting) and a failure on repeat, like the reflexive-comparison check.

No .NET change. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


